## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical Azure data pipeline design with beginner-friendly constraints, testing real-world implementation of data isolation, infrastructure as code, and CI/CD practices.

## Key Concepts

- Event Hubs for scalable event ingestion
- Per-tenant data isolation through Azure SQL schemas
- PII filtering and transformation with Azure Functions
- Infrastructure as Code using Bicep
- Continuous integration/deployment with GitHub Actions
- Cross-region disaster recovery via SQL Geo-Replication and RA-GRS
- Cost optimization: autoscaling, partition configuration, retention policies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation of routing logic for per-tenant data
function routeEvent(event){
  const tenantId = event.tenantId;
  // Filter PII and route to appropriate schema
  const filteredEvent = removePII(event);
  await writeToSQL(`tenant_${tenantId}`, filteredEvent);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates expertise in multi-region data residency, cross-tenant isolation-end governance spanning data and model lifec, and end-toycles in Azure.

## Key Concepts

- **Event Hubs**: Scalable ingestion from on-premises chat software
- **Synapse Spark**: Real-time NLP feature extraction (sentiment, entities, intent)
- **Delta Lake on ADLS Gen2**: Per-tenant isolation with secure access controls
- **Azure ML**: Centralized model registry with versioning and drift monitoring
- **Microsoft Purview**: Unified data governance and RBAC enforcement
- **BYOK via Key Vault**: Customer-managed encryption keys for compliance
- **Cross-region DR**: Paired region strategy with automated failover
- **Cost optimization**: Auto-scaling pools, reserved capacity, lifecycle policies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Register a model and trigger drift monitoring in Azure ML
async function registerModelAndMonitor(model, registry) {
  await registry.registerModel(model.name, model.version, { properties: { tenantId: model.tenantId } });
  const deployment = await registry.createDeployment(model.name, { computeType: 'aci' });
  await registry.enableDataDriftMonitoring(deployment, { baselineDataset: model.baseline, targetDataset: model.current });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Azure-native, multi-tenant data platform design under regulatory constraints with real-time processing, governance, security, disaster recovery, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant policy enforcement
- EU data residency with bring-your-own-key (BYOK) encryption
- Real-time event processing using Durable Functions
- Data governance with Purview and token-based sharing mechanisms
- Disaster recovery to paired region with automated failover strategies
- Cost optimization through serverless analytics, auto-scaling, and resource quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// Durable Function snippet: policy check and redaction (pseudo-code)
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const eventData = req.body;

  // Per-tenant policy validation
  const policy = await getTenantPolicy(tenantId);
  if (!validateEvent(eventData, policy)) {
    context.res = { status: 403, body: 'Policy violation' };
    return;
  }

  // PII redaction
  const redactedData = redactPII(eventData, policy.piiRules);

  // Store to ADLS and trigger downstream processing
  await storeToADLS(tenantId, redactedData);
  await triggerSynapseProcessing(tenantId, redactedData);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical knowledge of end-to-end IoT pipelines on Azure, including edge processing, streaming, and lakehouse analytics, plus security and cost controls.

## Key Concepts
- IoT Edge and IoT Hub integration
- Event Hubs as the streaming backbone
- Synapse lakehouse with Delta Lake for per-device isolation
- BYOK via Azure Key Vault; tenant/workspace scoping
- DR across regions and cost levers (retention, autoscale, tiering)

## Code Example
```javascript
const config = {
  ingestion: {
    edgeEnabled: true,
    hubName: 'iothub-prod',
    streamTo: 'eventhubs'
